<title>UK: Britain's VSEL axes 246 jobs.</title>
<headline>Britain's VSEL axes 246 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British shipbuilding and engineering company VSEL on Monday let go 246 white-collar workers.</p>
<p>The firm  blamed the decision on the running down of the Trident nuclear submarine programme. The cuts take to well below 5,000 the total number at the Barrow yard.</p>
<p>Five years ago when the Trident programme was at its peak, VSFL employed nearly three times as many workers.</p>
</text>
